# Every list the program consumes is rebuilt in its own cells: reverse
# turns each cell it visits around in place, body complements each
# character into the cell the input held it in, and splitAt, unrolled into
# putChunks for its constant count, gives each chunk the cells of its
# characters; and no walk counts a reference: the input is read into cells
# without a dup or a drop, and reverse neither counts nor tests one.
idr-rc: reuses-in-place=@Prelude.Types.List.reverseOnto counts-nothing=@Prelude.Types.List.reverseOnto tests-nothing=@Prelude.Types.List.reverseOnto counts-nothing=@Main.readAll reuses-in-place=@Main.body resets-unshared=@Main.body reuses-in-place=@Main.putChunks
